The Seven Wonders of the World project is a web-based project designed to provide information about the most famous and remarkable landmarks in the world.
These wonders represent human creativity, architectural excellence, cultural heritage, and historical importance.
The project presents details about each wonder in a simple, attractive, and user-friendly format.
The Seven Wonders included in this project are the Great Wall of China, Petra, Christ the Redeemer, Machu Picchu, Chichen Itza, the Colosseum, and the Taj Mahal.
Users can explore information about their location, history, architecture, and importance.
The main objective of this project is to create awareness about these extraordinary monuments and make learning about world heritage interesting through a digital platform. HTML, CSS, and JavaScript are used to develop the website and provide an interactive user experience.

